<title>ISRAEL: Israel May economic performance index up 0.4 pct. [CORRECTED 14:55 GMT]</title>
<headline>Israel May economic performance index up 0.4 pct. [CORRECTED 14:55 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel's economic performance</p>
<p>or &quot;S&quot; index rose 0.4 percent in May, the Bank of Israel said.</p>
<p>			     May 97   April 97     May 96</p>
<p>Month-on-month change   + 0.4   unchanged  - 0.5 Index (base 100=1994)</p>
<p>			 (Corrects to unchanged from +0.1)</p>
<p>				119.1   118.6	 116.6</p>
<p>			 (Corrects to 118.6 from 118.7)</p>
<p>The &quot;S&quot; index is made up of three components: retail sales, which fell 0.6 percent in May; imports, which rose 0.7 percent in May; and industrial production, which was unchanged in April.</p>
<p>Note: figures for industrial production lag one month.</p>
<p>- Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-2-537-2211</p>
